  "result": "No actions yet. I've already read the repo and have one question to ask first.\n\n---\n\nI looked through the app. Right now the timetable page is built from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no code for warnings. So the site currently has no way of knowing a sailing is off.\n\nThere's also a timing problem. Since the file only arrives once a night, a cancellation made that morning, for weather or a breakdown, wouldn't reach the site until after the sailing had already been missed. If same-day cancellations are the ones that matter most, the nightly file alone won't be enough.\n\nThat leaves one question that decides most of what gets built: **when a sailing is cancelled today, how does that news travel? Who decides it, and how do they tell people now?**",
